list.item:
The eLiebermann Lawcodes Database presents the laws clause by clause, according to Liebermann's own editorial divisions. It contains:


the Old English or Latin text as Liebermann prints it, labelled by manuscript;

Liebermann's German translation, with an English crib;

the texts and translations of later editors, where these are in the public domain;

Liebermann's textual notes and commentary;

a new subject index of offences, people and places;

cross-references between clauses, from Liebermann and later scholars, with citations.

The eLiebermann Legal Dictionary is a digital edition of Liebermann's Wörterbuch (volume II, part 1), the dictionary of the Old English, Latin and French words of the laws. It contains:


links for abbreviations and grammatical terms, with expansions and English translations;

links for law-code and manuscript sigla;

links from each law cited to its clause in the Lawcodes Database;

links to the works Liebermann cites;

links to entries in other dictionaries (in progress).

The eLiebermann Guide to the Gesetze expands and translates the apparatus of the Gesetze. It contains:


Liebermann's sigla for the law codes;

his list of manuscripts;

his grammatical terms and abbreviations;

the authors and works he cites;

his own account of how to read the dictionary;

his forewords, in German and English.
